  "title": "Factor covariance conditioned on 20% drawdown",
  "description": "This experiment conditions factor covariance on whether a capitalization-weighted excess-return proxy built from the permitted stocks is at least 20% below its observed running peak. Within the original 2,520-day window, it uses historical factor observations whose already-known proxy state matches the current state, retaining the original correlation and variance half-lives and full historical age gaps. If fewer than 63 matching days are available, it uses the original covariance. Exposures, specific risk, factor coefficients, stock forecasts and allocation remain original. This tests state-dependent risk estimation, not future knowledge of a downturn.",
